  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nMonday...Another day of building heat to potentially values needing \nanother heat headline, but with the same uncertainty of convection \nand associated debris limiting ambient temp warm up in places. Thus \nwill take heat headline issuance day-by-day. Right now for Monday \nand Monday night, the local area will continue under the storm track \nbut may be in between the more prime organized convective zones of \nthe northern/central plains and especially just off to the east of \nthe area extending to the eastern OH RVR Valley. Saying that, still \nplenty enough energy locally to fuel strong to severe storms if they \nget going. Bouts of heavy rain may also start to add up, as will be \nthe case into Thursday.\n\nTuesday through Saturday...With the flattening ridge transition, the \nlocal area may be under the battle zone of the LLVL thermal gradient \nand upper level short wave propagation path for almost daily chance \nof showers and storms for much of the week and even into the \nweekend. This deep summer-like MCS-track for much of the week from \nthe central plains over to the southern GRT LKS and OH RVR Valley \nmay add up to quite a bit of rainfall by Friday. At least temps look \ncooler by late week and into the weekend as well, with a day or two \npossibly held down in the 70s with cloud cover and east winds.",
